Z||000002||pHoOl||11-19-2000||10:19 PM||||Two questions for you.  <P>First, what is the MAP sensor?  I hear people talking about it all the time, but have no clue what it is.<P>Second, why keep your lights up the whole time?  Won't you end up getting water inside the housing leading to ice?  I've never heard of anybody keeping their retractable headlights up all through winter.  This is my first winter with my Fiero, so if it makes sense to do it, i suppose that i will.<P><BR>Sorry i couldn't help ya with anything.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-19-2000||10:29 PM||||M.A.P. = Manifold Air Pressure. It is the little black box on the back (trunk side) right of the intake plenum. Has an electrical connector and a vacuum line going into it.<P>I agree, I would'nt leave the lights up all winter, not a good idea. Also, the fan, I would just hook it to a differnt switch if I were you. Put a new switch under the dash or somthing. I would tend to think it should be automatically controlled because you could forget about it one of these days. I wouldnt think it would affect the car heating up all that much becuase the thermostat doesnt open until the engine gets hot, so coolant wont really begin flowing freely until the engine gets warm and opens it. The car should be allowed to warm up to normal operating temp because running it cool all the time will cause premature wear on engine parts. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||doughboySE||11-19-2000||10:30 PM||||first of all the map sensor hehe no idea but car runs great now<BR>and the reason for my lights up are because the last winter i drove it there were many morning the lights were closed and couldnt get them open. thats my reason anyway||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||11-20-2000||03:38 AM||||The reason to keep the lights up all the time is so you don't strip out a headlight gear because of an iced-up door.  It's a bigger problem than getting some water/ice in the light bucket area.  A lot less wear and tear on the motors that way, too.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||11-20-2000||09:21 PM||||But if you chip away the ice, and just monitor it, you should be alright huh?  Sounds like a deal to me.<P>Thanks for the info<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
